rather than being sent to market, are being discarded in bulk.

00:00:22.208 --> 00:00:26.125
Oh, yeah--I heard about that
on the news. What a waste!

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:30.167
Right? So I came up with a plan

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:30.292
"My Plan (Secret)"
Right? So I came up with a plan

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:34.125
"My Plan (Secret)"
to salvage those discarded eggs <i>and </i>assassinate Koro Sensei.

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:36.792
What, kill him with eggs?

00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:40.667
Bah. So you cook up a dish,
toss in some of these babies?

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.042
Like he won't see right through that.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.125
"My Plan (Secret)"

00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:46.417
"My Plan (Secret)"
I gave it a little more thought than that.

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:50.458
The first steps are already in place,
thanks to Mr. Karasuma.

00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:52.458
Yes, everything's all set up in the yard--

00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:55.292
To the yard, everyone!

00:00:55.292 --> 00:01:00.875
Honestly. These kids come up
with the craziest things.

00:01:03.625 --> 00:01:07.042
This mold... and those eggs... Don't tell me--

00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:11.917
Yep! We're going to make
one ginormous pudding!

00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:13.583
I call it...

00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:15.958
Operation Pudding Popper!

00:01:29.458 --> 00:01:32.125
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.958
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:01:34.958 --> 00:01:40.375
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:01:40.375 --> 00:01:43.042
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:01:43.042 --> 00:01:45.750
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.542
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:53.583
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:56.542
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:01:56.542 --> 00:02:01.750
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:07.333
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:12.750
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:18.250
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.875
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:02:20.875 --> 00:02:23.542
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:26.333
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:02:26.333 --> 00:02:28.917
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:02:28.917 --> 00:02:31.625
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:02:31.625 --> 00:02:34.375
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:02:34.375 --> 00:02:37.208
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:42.167
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.000
"Second Period: Kaede Time"
"by Tomohito Sugino"

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:56.708
Operation Pudding Popper?
Koro Sensei <i>does </i>have a sweet tooth...

00:02:56.708 --> 00:02:57.917
About that!

00:02:57.917 --> 00:03:01.000
I've already obtained a crucial confession!

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:01.917
"Pudding"
I've already obtained a crucial confession!

00:03:01.917 --> 00:03:04.833
"Pudding"
Couldn't you just eat a ton of these puddings?

00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:06.583
You bet I could!

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:10.708
Someday I'd love to dive into
a pudding that's bigger than me!

00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:14.583
I don't have the money,
so I guess it won't happen.

00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:17.167
Let's make his impossible dream come true!

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.542
Frankly, I'd like to eat some, too!

00:03:20.042 --> 00:03:23.000
--We'll embed bombs and anti-Sensei BB's
--Chomp chomp chomp chomp...

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.750
--in the giant pudding's base.
--Chomp chomp chomp chomp...

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:28.250
--When he gets to the bottom of the thing...
--Chomp chomp chomp chomp...

00:03:29.917 --> 00:03:31.833
It might be worth a try.

00:03:31.833 --> 00:03:35.917
He does tend to go crazy over sweets and sexy stuff.

00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:36.042
"My Plan (Secret)"
He does tend to go crazy over sweets and sexy stuff.

00:03:36.042 --> 00:03:39.792
"My Plan (Secret)"
And with behind-the-scenes Kayano stepping forward with this plan,

00:03:39.792 --> 00:03:41.167
"My Plan (Secret)"
there's an element of surprise, too.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:44.125
Okay, let's use this time
when Koro Sensei's not around

00:03:44.125 --> 00:03:45.292
and go for broke!

00:03:45.292 --> 00:03:46.917
Yeah!

00:03:51.542 --> 00:03:54.500
I used an inactive line at a mayonnaise factory

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:59.083
to prep the beaten eggs
that'll be going in this giant mold.

00:03:59.083 --> 00:04:01.417
But with cooperation from the government,

00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:05.917
we'll be doing the rest of
the cooking with our own manpower!

00:04:05.917 --> 00:04:09.250
First we mix in sugar and milk.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.167
Vanilla oil brings out the flavor.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:14.875
But, Kaede, they tried to
make a giant pudding on TV once,

00:04:14.875 --> 00:04:16.292
and it didn't work.

00:04:16.292 --> 00:04:16.625
"White Sugar"
and it didn't work.

00:04:16.625 --> 00:04:20.500
"White Sugar"
It was too big-- it collapsed under its own weight.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.333
"White Sugar"
To combat that,

00:04:22.333 --> 00:04:24.042
"White Sugar"
we're mixing in agar <i>and </i>gelatin as coagulants.

00:04:24.042 --> 00:04:25.917
we're mixing in agar <i>and </i>gelatin as coagulants.

00:04:25.917 --> 00:04:27.667
The agar's fiber will make it stronger.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:28.250
"White Sugar"
The agar's fiber will make it stronger.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:28.667
"Gelatin" "Agar" "In-house comparison"
The agar's fiber will make it stronger.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:33.625
"Gelatin" "Agar" "In-house comparison"
Plus, agar's higher melting point means it's slower to melt in heat,

00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:36.083
"Gelatin" "Agar" "In-house comparison"
so the pudding should stay firm even outside in September.

00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:37.875
"Gelatin" "Agar" "In-house comparison"
Whoa...

00:04:37.875 --> 00:04:40.708
Pour in the first batch of pudding!

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:50.042
That's the way! Once that's all in,
swap with Team Second Batch!

00:04:50.042 --> 00:04:50.625
"Cream Content" "Firmness" "Firm"

00:04:50.625 --> 00:04:51.542
"Cream Content" "Firmness" "Firm"
