00:04:58.042 --> 00:05:00.792
Then what are these?

00:05:00.792 --> 00:05:04.667
Bursts of flavor: fruit sauce
and mousse in edible starch wrappers.

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:07.292
Wouldn't you get sick of
the same flavor all the way through?

00:05:07.292 --> 00:05:12.042
Adding these in here and there
will provide some taste variety.

00:05:12.042 --> 00:05:16.417
Once the mold is full,
put on the lid and let it chill.

00:05:16.417 --> 00:05:19.417
The mold's outer walls
are equipped with a cooling function,

00:05:19.417 --> 00:05:24.708
and the pipes inside are flowing with coolant.

00:05:24.708 --> 00:05:29.625
A pudding this voluminous
needs to be cooled inside and out.

00:05:29.625 --> 00:05:31.000
Wow...

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.333
Just how much does Kayano
know about pudding, anyway?

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:39.083
She's got the scientific basis
<i>and </i>she's studied up on flavor!

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.125
Way to go, Kayano.

00:05:44.125 --> 00:05:45.917
You thought up and did all this yourself

00:05:45.917 --> 00:05:48.208
after seeing that article on eggs?

00:05:48.208 --> 00:05:49.333
Uh-huh!

00:05:49.333 --> 00:05:52.625
I mean, I've wanted to try it for a while.

00:05:52.625 --> 00:05:55.250
With the Ministry of Defense covering the cost,

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.917
I figured this was the perfect opportunity.

00:05:57.917 --> 00:06:02.083
Once I put my mind to something,
I just keep on rolling.

00:06:02.083 --> 00:06:06.917
Kayano's always behind us,
helping out on our assassinations.

00:06:06.917 --> 00:06:10.542
That's why I'd pegged her
as the supporting type.

00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:14.167
I had no idea that, given a plot
that played to her interests,

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:15.542
--she could be so fired up.

00:06:15.542 --> 00:06:17.833
--Another early start tomorrow!
--she could be so fired up.

00:06:21.875 --> 00:06:26.042
After chilling overnight,
we check to see if it's firmed up enough...

00:06:26.042 --> 00:06:28.417
then remove the cooling pipes.

00:06:30.042 --> 00:06:30.958
--Keep 'er coming, keep 'er coming...
--Next,

00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:34.625
--Keep 'er coming, keep 'er coming...
--we loosen the bolts holding on the lid...

00:06:34.625 --> 00:06:38.750
and blow air between
the mold and the pudding itself.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.208
Then... we release the external lock!

00:06:46.125 --> 00:06:50.083
Once the pudding's out of the mold,
we shore up the outside

00:06:50.083 --> 00:06:53.500
with softened gelatin and agar,

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.583
top it off with caramel sauce, made separately,

00:06:56.583 --> 00:06:59.542
lightly toast the surface, and...

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.875
We did it!

00:07:08.458 --> 00:07:10.542
Oh, man, it looks delicious!

00:07:10.542 --> 00:07:13.875
You forget there's a bomb under there!

00:07:13.875 --> 00:07:19.167
And so Kayano's giant
killer pudding was complete.

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:26.042
C-Can I really eat this whole thing?

00:07:26.042 --> 00:07:30.292
Oh, yeah, sure. I just wanted to
use up those discarded eggs.

00:07:30.292 --> 00:07:32.875
It was all Kayano's idea.

00:07:34.875 --> 00:07:36.458
Oh, Kayano!

00:07:36.458 --> 00:07:38.000
Well, see ya, Koro Sensei.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.250
We've got an English class to get to.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.167
Don't let any of it go to waste, now!

00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:46.958
I would never! Oh, it's a dream come true!

00:07:46.958 --> 00:07:48.792
Here I go!

00:07:48.792 --> 00:07:52.792
Kayano--we'll watch
the detonation from the hallway.

00:07:52.792 --> 00:07:55.042
Oh. Uh-huh.

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:57.542
Yum yum yum yum!

00:07:57.542 --> 00:08:00.000
--Yum yum yum yum!
--Look at him go...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.000
It's only a matter of time
before he reaches the bottom!

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.708
There's a surveillance camera in there, too,

00:08:05.708 --> 00:08:08.167
alongside the remote-controlled bomb.

00:08:08.167 --> 00:08:12.167
We detonate the bomb just as
the pudding around it is eaten:

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:16.333
the moment the screen
lightens slightly from pitch black.

00:08:18.375 --> 00:08:20.458
The pudding...

00:08:20.458 --> 00:08:21.792
exploding...

00:08:21.792 --> 00:08:23.500
Yum yum yum yum!

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:26.208
Yum yum yum yum!

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:32.833
It's got to be tastier with
the flavors changing midway.

00:08:32.833 --> 00:08:37.792
Hmm, I see: so I should use
a scale model to test its strength.

00:08:37.792 --> 00:08:41.125
Nooo! Another collapse!

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.042
Pudding...

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.875
No!

00:08:47.875 --> 00:08:51.125
The pudding I poured all
my heart into can't go blowing up!

00:08:51.125 --> 00:08:53.500
Hey, calm down, Kayano!

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.833
Don't get emotionally attached
to a damn pudding!

00:08:55.833 --> 00:08:58.708
--It was <i>made </i>to be blown to bits!
--No, we can't!

00:08:58.708 --> 00:09:00.625
We need to keep it in the yard forever, as a monument!

00:09:00.625 --> 00:09:02.417
"Still Life with Pudding" "by Kaede Kayano"
We need to keep it in the yard forever, as a monument!

00:09:02.417 --> 00:09:02.500
"Still Life with Pudding" "by Kaede Kayano"
It'll rot!

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.667
"Danger"
It'll rot!

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:06.792
Phew... Time for a break.

00:09:06.792 --> 00:09:11.458
I detected the faint smell of
a foreign object in with the deliciousness.

00:09:11.458 --> 00:09:14.833
The bomb! And the detonator's been detached!

00:09:14.833 --> 00:09:14.958
"Koro Sensei Flirts with Disaster!" "His Exit Route Explained!"
The bomb! And the detonator's been detached!

00:09:14.958 --> 00:09:17.500
"Koro Sensei Flirts with Disaster!" "His Exit Route Explained!"
I ate from caramel to pudding to dirt,

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:20.083
"Koro Sensei Flirts with Disaster!" "His Exit Route Explained!"
then tunneled through the ground and removed it.

00:09:21.875 --> 00:09:24.750
Did you set up the bomb, Takebayashi?

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:27.000
Your calculations were spot on,

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.750
but I picked up on the
distinctive scent of plastic explosive.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.208
Next time, pay attention
to any odor components, too.

00:09:35.208 --> 00:09:36.708
Yes, sir.

00:09:38.167 --> 00:09:41.458
And since you all worked together
to make this pudding,

00:09:41.458 --> 00:09:43.292
you should all eat it together!

00:09:43.292 --> 00:09:47.333
I've set aside nice clean portions for you.

00:09:47.333 --> 00:09:48.917
Foiled again.

00:09:48.917 --> 00:09:51.167
And it was such a good idea.

00:09:51.167 --> 00:09:55.083
However, eating eggs
that are meant to be discarded

00:09:55.083 --> 00:09:58.208
is, strictly speaking, a violation of economic rules.

00:09:58.208 --> 00:09:58.333
"New Civics"
is, strictly speaking, a violation of economic rules.

00:09:58.333 --> 00:10:00.333
"New Civics"
We'll consider that and the importance of food

00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:02.875
"New Civics"
in our next civics class.

00:10:02.875 --> 00:10:03.833
"New Civics"
Yes, sir.

00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:04.708
Yes, sir.

00:10:05.833 --> 00:10:08.167
Too bad, Kayano...

00:10:08.167 --> 00:10:10.167
Or do you feel better now?

00:10:11.125 --> 00:10:15.458
I didn't think you could be so hardcore.

00:10:15.458 --> 00:10:18.458
It was fun--and out of the ordinary, too.

00:10:20.667 --> 00:10:27.042
Not even your closest friends
get to see your true blade.

00:10:27.042 --> 00:10:28.792
I'll do it again.

00:10:28.792 --> 00:10:32.167
This is where a pudding fan
can be a top-notch assassin.

00:10:32.167 --> 00:10:35.958
I've got any number of
jiggly blades at my disposal!

00:10:35.958 --> 00:10:39.958
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Kaede Kayano"

00:10:57.917 --> 00:10:59.792
After the break,

00:10:59.792 --> 00:11:04.292
Mr. Karasuma really started
buckling down on training.

00:11:04.292 --> 00:11:08.000
Today's phys ed class consisted of parkour...

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.875
...turned Cops and Robbers.

00:11:09.875 --> 00:11:12.583
The cops were our
two most fearsome teachers.

00:11:12.583 --> 00:11:15.917
If we catch them all,
they get twice the homework.

00:11:15.917 --> 00:11:18.000
Quit finding weird ways to piggyback on this.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:21.167
Aw, why can't I play, too?

00:11:21.167 --> 00:11:24.875
It's not fair--you guys have all the fun.

00:11:24.875 --> 00:11:27.583
Besides, I'm in charge of defense.

00:11:27.583 --> 00:11:31.458
Of course. It would hardly be
training with you on the chase.

00:11:31.458 --> 00:11:33.333
Even if it is Mr. Karasuma chasing us,

00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:35.417
this is one big mountainside!

00:11:35.417 --> 00:11:38.958
Given the time limit,
he'll only be able to tag...

00:11:38.958 --> 00:11:40.750
...two or three of us, max.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:42.208
Yep.

00:11:42.208 --> 00:11:43.958
I heard that.

00:11:43.958 --> 00:11:47.792
Beyond the ridgeline--at eighty meters.

00:11:54.542 --> 00:11:57.583
You're under arrest.

00:11:57.583 --> 00:11:59.083
--Huh?
--What?

00:11:59.792 --> 00:12:04.583
Okajima, Hayami, Chiba, Fuwa! Out!

00:12:04.583 --> 00:12:06.375
"Jail"
No lie--he's actually making us do drills in jail!

00:12:06.375 --> 00:12:09.375
No lie--he's actually making us do drills in jail!

00:12:09.375 --> 00:12:10.042
Say what?

00:12:10.042 --> 00:12:11.708
Now, look, Okajima...

00:12:11.708 --> 00:12:15.292
Not even realizing you were tagged?
What is this, some battle movie?

00:12:15.292 --> 00:12:19.750
Just be careful, okay?
He might already be behind you...

00:12:20.708 --> 00:12:23.500
Sugaya? Sugayaaa!

00:12:24.958 --> 00:12:27.250
Karasuma's on the hunt alone?

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:31.958
Perfect. I'll pull him in by his
tagging hand and take him down.

00:12:31.958 --> 00:12:36.833
Then we'll go at it right here.
I'll make a <i>real bad </i>cop out of him!

00:12:36.833 --> 00:12:39.167
I say bring it on! Oh, YE--

00:12:41.333 --> 00:12:44.750
Sugaya, Professor Bitch! Out!

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.833
Yikes. We're dropping like flies!

00:12:46.833 --> 00:12:49.042
It's like Mount Slaughter out here.

00:12:49.042 --> 00:12:50.542
Weren't they arrested?

00:12:50.542 --> 00:12:54.250
Oh--this is Cops and Robbers, right?
Which means...

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:57.417
Right! If we tag 'em, they're free!

00:12:57.417 --> 00:13:00.000
Sugino, you dummy.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.500
Like anyone's getting tagged
without that sonic octopus noticing.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:07.542
--Prisoners! Focus on your work detail, now!
--If we could do that, we would have killed him ages ago.

00:13:07.542 --> 00:13:10.333
You have a point.

00:13:10.333 --> 00:13:11.708
Sugino! Did you come to spring us?

00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:13.750
"Do something to Sensei!"
Sugino! Did you come to spring us?

00:13:16.083 --> 00:13:17.583
What?

00:13:21.458 --> 00:13:22.667
Just this once.

00:13:22.667 --> 00:13:25.083
Sugino! Now!

00:13:26.333 --> 00:13:28.625
"Officer Koro Scandal: Bribery"

00:13:28.625 --> 00:13:29.333
Five prisoners have escaped!

00:13:29.333 --> 00:13:30.125
"Escaped"
Five prisoners have escaped!

00:13:30.125 --> 00:13:31.125
"Escaped"
What?!

00:13:31.125 --> 00:13:35.083
Hey! How are these
captured robbers getting out?

00:13:35.083 --> 00:13:37.167
They're shrewder than I thought.

